# ---------- Claude Code local state ----------
.claude/settings.local.json
# CLAUDE.md was here, as local scratch. It is now the opposite: the
# rules an agent needs before it touches this repository, and the one
# that matters most - that a push has to reach two remotes - was living
# only in one person's machine-local memory, which does not load for a
# teammate, a different checkout, or a different tool. Tracked on
# purpose; do not put anything machine-specific or secret in it.

# Local dev stack: PID files and server logs (scripts/dev_stack.sh)
.run/

# Agent tooling state (oh-my-claudecode, oh-my-codex). Operational scratch, not code.
.omc/
.omx/

# ---------- uv lockfile ----------
# Removed from the repo 2026-08-12, not merely ignored. It was eight lines
# declaring the virtual root package and ZERO dependencies, while
# docker/requirements-api.txt pins twenty. A tracked lockfile that resolves
# to nothing is worse than none: `uv sync` succeeds, installs nothing, and
# the failure surfaces later as an ImportError nobody connects to it.
# requirements.txt is this project's single source of truth for deps. If uv
# is ever adopted properly, generate the lockfile from those pins and drop
# this rule in the same commit.
uv.lock

# ---------- README backup ----------
# The README was rewritten 2026-08-24; the previous one is kept on disk
# while the new one settles. Ignored rather than committed: two READMEs in
# the tree is two answers to "what is this project", and a reader who finds
# the stale one has no way to tell which is current. Delete it once nothing
# is being copied back out of it.
README.old.md
build/
dist/
artifacts/analyst-experiments/
